Canonical [Shell](../scripts/campaign/shell.gd) `_pause_at_barrier`120 delegates `request_pause`114 to `_enqueue("pause")`; its real menu is CampaignMenu. `_perform` pause path records the live snapshot and calls `menu.show_pause`, while canonical HUD overlay remains hidden. The 492 fixture correctly uses CampaignMenu in `_gui_resume_pair`242–256 and `_full_pause`258–262, but those overrides do not replace the inherited HUD predicate. Thus the hash-only source update cannot pass the first canonical pause barrier. A paused action clock also cannot consume `_wait`'s simulation deadline; its existing ten-minute outer watchdog remains the eventual bound. The checkpoint drain/resume guard must likewise remain canonical and separately observed.

Required next amendment is a distinct reviewed fixture-only capture-barrier override using the actual current CampaignMenu predicate, the original complete current framing readiness and same whole-tick/native-window semantics. Preserve all source/HP/body/clock/pause/recognizer/quiet/event/assertion boundaries; no forcing Resume, hidden HUD repair, fake source gate or timeout weakening. The contract helper owns that proposal. This recipe does not author it or change the hash-only492. Freeze its final amended source hash before recording/import/testing.

